Here are the final, production-ready configurations. Copy and paste these exactly as they are to resolve the UAT connection pool issues and safely run both databases concurrently under heavy load.

### 1. Oracle Configuration (Primary Database)

Replace the contents of `OracleDbConfig.java` with this code. It enforces the use of the HikariCP connection pool and links it to your properties file.

**File:** `src/main/java/com/fincore/VoucherService/config/OracleDbConfig.java`

```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.config;

import com.zaxxer.hikari.HikariDataSource;
import org.springframework.boot.context.properties.ConfigurationProperties;
import org.springframework.boot.jdbc.DataSourceBuilder;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Primary;

import javax.sql.DataSource;

@Configuration
public class OracleDbConfig {

    @Primary
    @Bean(name = "oracleDataSource")
    @ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "spring.datasource")
    public DataSource oracleDataSource() {
        return DataSourceBuilder.create().type(HikariDataSource.class).build();
    }
}

```

---

### 2. Hive Configuration (Secondary Database)

Replace the contents of `HiveConfig.java` with this code. Notice there is no `@Primary` annotation, and it uses a unique property prefix so it doesn't clash with Oracle.

**File:** `src/main/java/com/fincore/VoucherService/config/HiveConfig.java`

```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.config;

import com.zaxxer.hikari.HikariDataSource;
import org.springframework.boot.context.properties.ConfigurationProperties;
import org.springframework.boot.jdbc.DataSourceBuilder;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

import javax.sql.DataSource;

@Configuration
public class HiveConfig {

    @Bean(name = "hiveDataSource")
    @ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "spring.hive.datasource")
    public DataSource hiveDataSource() {
        return DataSourceBuilder.create().type(HikariDataSource.class).build();
    }
}

```

